# Blocks and retag (codegen 2.0 rules, enforced by `bun tools/lint-apps.ts` in `bun run check`)

The detectors are the codegen 2.0 `rules` group (`packages/ui/.xgen/xgen/check/src/rules`), run on composition code of `apps/site/views`, `apps/design-svelte/src`, `apps/design-react/src` and the generated `packages/blocks/{svelte,react,templ}`.

- **block-root.** `Block` is the only unit for page sections, landmarks and public anchors. Retag it by meaning: `tag: "section" | "header" | "footer" | "nav" | "main" | "aside" | "article" | "figure" | "search" | "hgroup"`.
  - At most one Block per render path; exclusive `if/else` branches may each have one. Never nest a Block in a Block, never put one in a loop: extract a file (for example `NavTree`, `ShowcasePart`).
  - A page (`+page.svelte`, `src/pages/*.tsx`) and every generated block opens on Block, directly or through a component whose file opens on Block (`PageHeader`).
- **raw-native-tag.** No raw HTML tags in composition. Use primitives with `tag`/`as`:
  - `Container tag="main"`, `Block tag="nav"`, `Title as={2}`.
  - `Text tag="blockquote" | "time" | "figcaption"`, `Inline` for `span`.
  - `List`/`ListItem`, `Table*`, `LinkPlain` for a bare `<a>`.
  - Allowed tags per primitive are in codegen `utils/tags`; do not widen them. The templ document shell (`apps/site/views/layout.templ`) may use `html head body meta title link script`.
- **raw-html.** No `{@html}`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or `@templ.Raw` in composition.
  - Icons are components: Go `@icons.Icon(name, class)`, Svelte `<Icon name class />` (`@saas-design/icons/svelte`), React `<Icon name className />`.
  - The one raw write of an icon is inside `packages/icons`.
- **dynamic-tag.** No `<svelte:element this>` or computed host tags. Region slots in templ use `@templ.Join(r.Main...)`.
- **reactive-aria.** ARIA state (`aria-current`, `aria-expanded`, ...) is never an expression. Write a static attribute in each branch (see `NavTree`) or pass the state through a primitive prop.
- **inline-style** (this repo). No `style` attribute anywhere.
- **literal-text.** Blocking in blocks: their copy comes from fixtures. Report-only in the docs apps.
- **Baseline.** An accepted finding goes in `tools/lint-apps.baseline.json` with a reason. It is matched by file + detector + message, and a stale entry fails. Prefer fixing the code over adding an entry.
- **Anchors.** `id` / anchors belong to `Block` (or `Container tag="section"` inside a page), plus primitives that own ids (Field/Input, Button, Form, Dialog, Disclosure, Output, Meter, Progress). Sections use `aria-labelledby` pointing to their `Title` id.
- **Box.** `Box` is internal layout only (no anchors, no landmarks). Inside a Block compose with `Container`, `Stack`, `Group`, `Grid`, `Card`, list/table/media/disclosure/form primitives.
- **Headings.** One `Title as={1}` per page (hero); section titles `as={2}`, card titles `as={3}`.
- **DSL.** Blocks are defined once in `packages/blocks/defs` with the DSL and emitted to templ, Svelte and React. Use `c(...)` for primitives and `h(...)` only for tags no primitive owns; `h` is reported by the lint. Block parity in `bun run check` must report 0 mismatches.
- **Catalog.** Max 45 blocks. Each block has `id`, `category`, `description`, a `figma` node ref (or catalog-only), a data schema, and fixture data in `fixtures/views/blocks.json`.
